[node:accd44a8-dbbc-42b1-9619-d523f963d636]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/a-bak-copy-takes-part-in-no-git-sync
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:13:42.752986+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:b631c2f3-9c9e-4575-b9de-3a8d62cf7e10] @ 2026-09-06T11:13:42.752986+00:00

A `.bak` copy takes part in no git sync, in either direction (sync.is_backup). Path.with_suffix maps memory-graph.db.bak to memory-graph.db.dump — one character from the tracked memory-graph.dump — so writing to a backup used to publish a phantom dump beside the real one (the unexplained file in issue #5), and a newer such dump would have rebuilt the backup from it, destroying the copy someone opened to rescue data.
---
