[node:8c7019d2-df1b-4e4e-8642-21e6aa1d5480]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/id-not-in-null-is-null-for-every-row
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:27:22.463303+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:c7bdc219-b9f2-4f03-8bf8-0588e4468eac] @ 2026-09-06T11:27:22.463303+00:00

`id NOT IN (NULL)` is NULL for every row in SQLite, so a NOT IN exclusion built from an empty list silently filters out everything it was meant to preserve. Omit the clause entirely when the list is empty; the positive `IN (NULL)` form is safe.
---
